| S_T^γ bin (GeV) | Weighted yield |
|----------------|----------------|
| 600–800         | 0.502          |
| 800–1000        | 1.783          |
| 1000–1300       | 6.092          |
| > 1300          | **50.654**     |
| **Total**       | **59.03**      |

**Key fix made this session:** The LHE file header had `DECAY 1000022 0.000000e+00` (chi10 total width = 0), causing Pythia to treat the NLSP as stable. All 16 LHE chunk files were patched to `DECAY 1000022 1.000000e+00`, enabling chi10 → γ G̃ decays. After re-showering (50000 events, 16 parallel jobs), re-running Delphes, and re-running analysis, 68.8% of events now have reconstructed photons (vs. 5.4% before the fix), and 53.2% of generated events pass all signal region cuts.

The distribution is dominated by the >1300 GeV bin because for m(χ̃₁⁰) = 1700 GeV, the photon from χ̃₁⁰ → γG̃ carries ~850 GeV in the NLSP rest frame, and two gravitinos produce large MET, so S_T^γ typically exceeds 1300 GeV.
